{
  "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
  "format-version": "0.1",
  "name": "biomni_genomics_unsupervised_celltype_transfer_between_scRNA_datasets",
  "annotation": "Transfer cell type labels from an annotated reference scRNA-seq dataset to an unannotated query dataset using popV. Loads both AnnData .h5ad files, prepares count layers for scVI, processes the query against the reference, and runs selected annotation methods (default: SCANVI_POPV). Saves predictions to 'output_folder/popv_output/predictions.csv'. This function allows you to use different annotaiton methods i.e. CELLTYPIST, KNN_BBKNN, KNN_HARMONY, KNN_SCANORAMA, KNN_SCVI, ONCLASS, Random_Forest, SCANVI_POPV, Support_Vector, XGboost. Based on you transfer task you can select the multiple best annotation methods. Beware each annotation method adds computational requirements for running the tool. By default it uses SCANVI_POPV method.",
  "tags": [
    "biomni",
    "genomics",
    "single-step"
  ],
